1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
In order to make it easier for users to create hair loss results, we launched the hair loss vinegar generator in the 2024.2 version.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
By using this function, users can self-define and generate multiple hair loss results.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:28,000
In addition, in order to improve usability, we also provided 15 hair loss predictions in the Connect business city, so that users can directly use them.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
In this video, I will introduce the hair loss vinegar generator in detail and how to apply the hair loss that it wants to generate.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
First, open the project file.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The hair loss prediction adjusted from the Connect or pre-adjusted by yourself will be dragged to the object window and applied on the board.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Select the hair loss material.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:55,000
In the property editor, before opening the hair loss generator, the basic parameters such as hair material, hair type, and so on have been set.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Then pull the scroll down.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Find the default image.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Click on the hair loss next to the default image.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Open the window of the hair loss generator.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
In the hair loss generator, there are two default images, the long-distance image and the curved-direction image.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:18,000
You can adjust the long-distance image and the curved-direction image to easily generate hair loss.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Click on the long-distance image and the curved-direction image with the mouse to see the long-distance image and the curved-direction image.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
On the left is the corresponding default preview effect,

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
and on the right is the adjustable attribute.

18
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
These parameters can be adjusted in any way,

19
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
and can be previewed on the left to check the default effect generated.

20
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
First, let's come to the length chart.

21
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Under the attributes on the right of the length chart,

22
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
there are two attributes, including the cutting chart and the editing effect.

23
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
If these two attributes are not displayed on the menu,

24
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
you can click on the small triangle on the left.

25
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Cutting chart and editing effect, these two attributes,

26
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
are used to set the length effect of hair vinegar.

27
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
First, let's look at the cutting chart.

28
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
The cutting chart is mainly used to show different lengths of hair in the same texture pattern.

29
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
It contains the mode, image level,

30
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
low area length and high area length four parameters.

31
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Currently, the four parameters are gray.

32
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
To make it adjustable,

33
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
the cutting chart must be added here.

34
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Next, let's explain each parameter separately.

35
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
To better understand and apply.

36
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
First is the mode.

37
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
It includes RGB and alpha modes.

38
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Select RGB10.

39
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The length of the hair depends on the grayness of the cutting chart.

40
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
The cutting chart needs to use gray.

41
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Among them, the black area indicates the lowest hair length.

42
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The white area indicates the highest hair length.

43
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
If you choose the alpha mode,

44
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
the length of the hair depends on the transparency of the cutting chart.

45
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
The cutting chart needs to apply transparency.

46
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
The transparent area indicates the lowest hair length.

47
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
The non-transparent area indicates the highest hair length.

48
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Next, let's look at the image level.

49
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
It can adjust the intensity of gray.

50
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Increasing the value can make the cut effect more obvious.

51
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Next is the length of the low area and the length of the high area.

52
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,000
These two parameters can adjust the shortest and longest hair length.

53
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Next, let's look at the editing effect.

54
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
The editing effect includes intensity and randomness.

55
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Let's look at the intensity first.

56
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
The higher the intensity value,

57
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
the greater the difference in hair length from the edge to the center.

58
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
This creates a sharper hair hair.

59
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
The intensity below is random.

60
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,000
It can adjust whether the length of the hair on the entire surface of the fabric is consistent or irregular.

61
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,000
The higher the value, the more inconsistent the length of the hair hair.

62
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
And the long and short hair hair distribution is also irregular.

63
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Next, let's look at the curve distribution.

64
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Let's look at the curve direction chart.

65
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,000
It includes two properties, hair loss and hair loss details.

66
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
First, click on hair loss.

67
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Hair loss makes the hair show the effect of one hair.

68
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:07,000
It contains intensity, hair loss density, random direction, intensity, and random four parameters.

69
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Next, let's explain the meaning of each parameter separately.

70
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
To better understand and apply.

71
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
First is the intensity.

72
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:19,000
The property can adjust the intensity of the hair on each direction of the curve.

73
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,000
The higher the intensity, the more obvious the hair loss, the stronger the three-dimensional effect.

74
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Next is the density of hair loss.

75
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,000
It can adjust the density of hair loss.

76
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
The higher the value, the higher the density of hair loss.

77
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
The smaller the hair loss, the closer it is.

78
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
The smaller the value, the lower the density of hair loss.

79
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
The larger the hair loss, the more scattered it is.

80
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
About random direction and random intensity.

81
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:48,000
These two parameters can set the curve direction of hair loss adjustment.

82
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
It is consistent or irregular.

83
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Next, let's click on hair loss details.

84
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Hair loss details are used to adjust the detail effect of each hair loss.

85
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
It contains five parameters.

86
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
The function meaning of the first four parameters is similar to what is said above.

87
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
There is no more explanation.

88
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Finally, the intensity of hair loss is increased.

89
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,000
It can adjust the concentration of each hair loss.

90
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
At the same time, the direction of each hair loss remains unchanged.

91
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
The intensity of hair loss is higher.

92
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
It is correct for hair loss.

93
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:23,000
With the highest density setting, it can be made the hair loss smooth and loose.

94
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
It's like being tidied up.

95
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Next, we will follow the meaning of the attributes parameters as described in the previous video.

96
